{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 3317 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8b7e86b68cf67e9eaf3c5c70db22e4b1ed6ffb96c207c50dcd68a1e164f92a61" :edb/db-before-t 3316 :edb/db-after-t 3317 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536629 50 #inst "2026-10-17T04:19:58.253Z" 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186054604 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575527 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186054664 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575582 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186059638 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575561 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186059865 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575601 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186059975 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064178 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575596 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064179 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575621 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064180 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575547 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064181 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575586 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064281 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575597 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575598 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064283 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575558 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064392 1050 420.0 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064405 1050 900.0 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186064558 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186065335 1064 "The chain rule can be used to differentiate trigonometric functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\sin (2x).\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\sin u, \\qquad u = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{cos}(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536629 17592186045417 false] [17592186065335 1064 "The chain rule can be used to differentiate trigonometric functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\sin (2x).\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\sin u, \\qquad u = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186065409 1064 "We know that the derivative of sine is cosine:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(\\sin{x}) = \\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSince integration is the reverse of differentiation, we see that the integral of cosine is sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\sin{x} + C\n$$\n\nWe can discover two other integrals by considering the derivatives of cosine and tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}x+C \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{tan}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, by considering the derivatives of secant, cosecant, and cotangent, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}x+C \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}x+C \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cot}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith these six formulas, we can integrate many different trigonometric functions." 13194139536629 17592186045417 false] [17592186065409 1064 "We know that the derivative of sine is cosine:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(\\sin{x}) = \\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSince integration is the reverse of differentiation, we see that the integral of cosine is sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\sin{x} + C\n$$\n\nWe can discover two other integrals by considering the derivatives of cosine and tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, by considering the derivatives of secant, cosecant, and cotangent, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith these six formulas, we can integrate many different trigonometric functions." 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068857 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575583 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068857 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575595 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068857 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575603 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068858 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575615 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068858 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575618 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575581 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575600 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575620 13194139536629 17592186045417 true] [17592186068859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186575623 1319413953